ADDENDA <Presidential Decree No. 33251, Feb. 16, 2023>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Decree shall enter into force on the date of its promulgation.
Article 2 (Repeal of other statutes or regulations)
The Enforcement Decree of the Special Act on Assistance in Development of Local Newspapers (Presidential Decree No. 18559) (including the portions amended by the Partial Amendment to the Enforcement Decree of the Special Act on Assistance in Development of Local Newspapers (Presidential Decree No. 32183)) shall be repealed.
Article 3 (Transitional measures concerning non-standing expert members of Subcommittees)
A part-time expert appointed under Article 4 (2) of the former Enforcement Decree of the Special Act on Assistance in Development of Local Newspapers (referring to the one repealed under Article 2 of the Addenda; hereinafter the same shall apply) shall be deemed to have been appointed under Article 6 (2).
Article 4 (Transitional measures concerning detailed operating rules)
The operating rules established by the chairperson through a resolution of the Committee pursuant to Article 6 of the Enforcement Decree of the Special Act on Assistance in Development of Local Newspapers shall be deemed to be established by the chairperson through a resolution of the Committee pursuant to Article 8.
Article 5 (Transitional measures concerning Local Newspapers Development Fund Account)
The Local Newspaper Development Fund Account established under Article 7 of the Enforcement Decree of the Special Act on Assistance in Development of Local Newspapers shall be deemed to have been established under Article 9.
Article 6 (Transitional measures concerning accounting agency of Fund)
Where the head of a Fund trustee institution has appointed a director in charge of Fund revenues, a director in charge of Fund expenditure authorization, a staff member in charge of Fund expenditures, and a staff member in charge of Fund receipts and disbursements, and has reported such fact to the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism under the former part of Article 9 (1) of the former Enforcement Decree of the Special Act on the Promotion of Local Newspapers, such act shall be deemed to constitute the appointment of a director in charge of Fund revenues, a director in charge of Fund expenditure authorization, a staff member in charge of Fund expenditures, and a staff member in charge of Fund receipts and disbursements, and the reporting thereof, by the head of the Fund trustee institution pursuant to the former part of Article 11 (1).
Article 7 (Transitional measures concerning detailed criteria for preferential support)
The details of the criteria for priority support determined by the chairperson with the resolution of the Committee pursuant to Article 13 (2) of the former Enforcement Decree of the Special Act on Assistance in Development of Local Newspapers shall be deemed to have been determined by the chairperson with the resolution of the Committee pursuant to Article 16 (2).
Article 8 (Relationship to other statutes and regulations)
Where any other statute cites the former Enforcement Decree of Special Act on Assistance in Development of Local Newspapers or any provision thereof at the time this Decree enters into force, such references shall be deemed references to this Decree or the relevant provisions thereof in lieu of the former Decree or provisions.
